&HEAD CHID='apollo_cm012_ug', TITLE='Apollo Command Module CM-012 - 100 % O2 - 16.7 psia - 0 g' /

Generated by FIREFALL (web/src/fds/toFds.ts) from cabin.yaml, materials.csv and cabin.model.json.
Model y-up is FDS z-up. Rotated parts are their axis-aligned bounding boxes. The hull cone is voxelised
into stepped solid blocks so the cabin is a sealed volume and FDS computes the pressure rise itself.
Surface data are air cone-calorimeter values: in 100 % O2 real burning is faster, so this is a lower bound.

&MESH IJK=40,40,32, XB=-2,2,-2,2,0,3.2 /
&TIME T_END=30 /
&MISC P_INF=115142., TMPA=22., GVEC=0.,0.,0 /
&DUMP DT_DEVC=0.25, DT_HRR=0.25, DT_SLCF=0.5, DT_SMOKE3D=0.5, DT_RESTART=1000000. /

Cabin atmosphere 100 % O2 at 16.7 psia. Fuel: ethylene surrogate, soot yield 0.05.
&SPEC ID='OXYGEN', BACKGROUND=.TRUE. /
&SPEC ID='ETHYLENE' /
&SPEC ID='CARBON DIOXIDE' /
&SPEC ID='WATER VAPOR' /
&SPEC ID='SOOT' /
&REAC FUEL='ETHYLENE', HEAT_OF_COMBUSTION=25000.,
      SPEC_ID_NU='ETHYLENE','OXYGEN','CARBON DIOXIDE','WATER VAPOR','SOOT',
      NU=-1.,-2.88322,1.88322,2.,0.11678 /

Nylon 6,6 fabric: Babrauskas, Ignition Handbook (2003) tables 14-15; SFPE Handbook 5th ed. ch. 26 (cone calorimeter, air)
&MATL ID='NYLON', DENSITY=1140., CONDUCTIVITY=0.24, SPECIFIC_HEAT=1.7 /
&SURF ID='NYLON', COLOR='ORANGE', MATL_ID='NYLON', THICKNESS=0.0005, HRRPUA=800., IGNITION_TEMPERATURE=430. /
Cotton fabric: Babrauskas, Ignition Handbook (2003) tables 14-15; SFPE Handbook 5th ed. ch. 26 (cone calorimeter, air)
&MATL ID='COTTON', DENSITY=300., CONDUCTIVITY=0.06, SPECIFIC_HEAT=1.3 /
&SURF ID='COTTON', COLOR='KHAKI', MATL_ID='COTTON', THICKNESS=0.001, HRRPUA=200., IGNITION_TEMPERATURE=260. /
PMMA / PU foam pad: Babrauskas, Ignition Handbook (2003) tables 14-15; SFPE Handbook 5th ed. ch. 26 (cone calorimeter, air)
&MATL ID='PMMA', DENSITY=1190., CONDUCTIVITY=0.19, SPECIFIC_HEAT=1.42 /
&SURF ID='PMMA', COLOR='LIGHT BLUE', MATL_ID='PMMA', THICKNESS=0.006, HRRPUA=650., IGNITION_TEMPERATURE=300. /
PTFE wire insulation: Babrauskas, Ignition Handbook (2003) tables 14-15; SFPE Handbook 5th ed. ch. 26 (cone calorimeter, air)
&MATL ID='TEFLON', DENSITY=2200., CONDUCTIVITY=0.25, SPECIFIC_HEAT=1 /
&SURF ID='TEFLON', COLOR='WHITE', MATL_ID='TEFLON', THICKNESS=0.001, HRRPUA=20., IGNITION_TEMPERATURE=560. /
Silicone rubber seal: Babrauskas, Ignition Handbook (2003) tables 14-15; SFPE Handbook 5th ed. ch. 26 (cone calorimeter, air)
&MATL ID='SILICONE', DENSITY=1200., CONDUCTIVITY=0.22, SPECIFIC_HEAT=1.3 /
&SURF ID='SILICONE', COLOR='PINK', MATL_ID='SILICONE', THICKNESS=0.005, HRRPUA=150., IGNITION_TEMPERATURE=450. /
&SURF ID='HULL', COLOR='GRAY 60' /
&SURF ID='STRUCTURE', COLOR='GRAY 40' /

Pressure hull: shell (cone r 1.95 -> 0.45 m over 3.2 m), voxelised at 0.1 m.
