Ignition: ecu-wiring (Damaged wiring near the environmental control unit (most probable source)) - a 75 kW burner, off at 20 s,
placed under the nearest listed burnable item: Debris nets (0.4 m from the fault).
&SURF ID='IGNITER', COLOR='RED', HRRPUA=833.3, RAMP_Q='IGN' /
&RAMP ID='IGN', T=0., F=0. /
&RAMP ID='IGN', T=1., F=1. /
&RAMP ID='IGN', T=20., F=1. /
&RAMP ID='IGN', T=21., F=0. /
&OBST ID='BURNER', XB=-0.6,-0.3,0.2,0.5,0.2,0.3, SURF_ID='STRUCTURE' /
&VENT ID='IGNITER', XB=-0.6,-0.3,0.2,0.5,0.3,0.3, SURF_ID='IGNITER' /

Smoke detectors from cabin.yaml. FDS uses the Cleary two-parameter lag model on chamber obscuration;
it sees soot mass, not particle size, so it cannot tell ionization from photoelectric sensitivity to small smoke.
&PROP ID='ionization', QUANTITY='CHAMBER OBSCURATION', ALPHA_E=2.5, BETA_E=-0.7, ALPHA_C=0.8, BETA_C=-0.9, ACTIVATION_OBSCURATION=3.24 /
&PROP ID='photoelectric', QUANTITY='CHAMBER OBSCURATION', ALPHA_E=1.8, BETA_E=-1.1, ALPHA_C=1.0, BETA_C=-0.8, ACTIVATION_OBSCURATION=3.24 /
&DEVC ID='D1', PROP_ID='ionization', XYZ=0,0,2.7 / ionization - console
&DEVC ID='D2', PROP_ID='photoelectric', XYZ=1.45,0,0.55 / photoelectric - couches
&DEVC ID='P_cabin', QUANTITY='BACKGROUND PRESSURE', XYZ=0.,0.,1.6 /
&DEVC ID='O2_cabin', QUANTITY='VOLUME FRACTION', SPEC_ID='OXYGEN', XYZ=0.,0.,1.6 /
&DEVC ID='TC_0.45', QUANTITY='TEMPERATURE', XYZ=0.,0.,0.45 /
&DEVC ID='TC_0.85', QUANTITY='TEMPERATURE', XYZ=0.,0.,0.85 /
&DEVC ID='TC_1.25', QUANTITY='TEMPERATURE', XYZ=0.,0.,1.25 /
&DEVC ID='TC_1.65', QUANTITY='TEMPERATURE', XYZ=0.,0.,1.65 /
&DEVC ID='TC_2.05', QUANTITY='TEMPERATURE', XYZ=0.,0.,2.05 /
&DEVC ID='TC_2.45', QUANTITY='TEMPERATURE', XYZ=0.,0.,2.45 /
&DEVC ID='TC_2.85', QUANTITY='TEMPERATURE', XYZ=0.,0.,2.85 /

&SLCF PBY=0., QUANTITY='TEMPERATURE' /
&SLCF PBY=0., QUANTITY='DENSITY', SPEC_ID='SOOT' /
&SLCF PBZ=1.15, QUANTITY='TEMPERATURE' /

&TAIL /
